    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cdc1e9ce1d104aff9f6405855933076a",
      "statement": "The TypeSafeClient bean used by the Jev integration is built in config/TypeSafeConfig on a clone() of the shared auto-configured RestClient.Builder, with its own Reactor Netty ClientHttpRequestFactory carrying Jev-specific timeouts (5s connect, spring.ai.typesafe.timeout read), so Jev calls get an isolated transport while still inheriting the shared User-Agent customizer and observation instrumentation from the cloned builder.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/config/TypeSafeConfig.java#L43-L61",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1df96af2ef284f64c92c13fb281d6c728ad25754ab12e714b97c43ebaadd9360:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f18be86648674bb0b2ed8cdcc0801d9b",
      "statement": "config/TypeSafeConfig defines the TypeSafeClient bean itself (rather than relying on the TypeSafe starter's own bean) so that a blank or missing MYFEEDER_TYPESAFE_API_KEY only disables interest scoring via a log message instead of crashing application startup, because the starter's own bean would otherwise assert the API key has text.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/config/TypeSafeConfig.java#L23-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b46d6e675f7853ae8957f068081841f0385834ae5edb9d4f93bf0fea780734ca:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d5c36036b4b349efab8c9ae0d24e00dd",
      "statement": "The shared auto-configured RestClient.Builder uses a Reactor Netty transport (ReactorClientHttpRequestFactory) pinned by an explicit reactor-netty-http dependency, and carries a myfeeder/<version> User-Agent set by RestClientConfig's RestClientCustomizer bean, which Spring Boot auto-applies to every RestClient.Builder built from that shared instance (e.g. for FeedFetcher and RaindropApiClientImpl).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CLAUDE.md#L272-L272",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5f35daa8419caedc2b42ac64af0fb12783a925584e11f98893e421e04a26d980:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/config/RestClientConfig.java",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:59e251d92d80154e8321de8893781b8485360b3008daaa1aa931a7fb1ede2cb3"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_261c35d42c2a4234bdfaef5fa68023e7",
      "statement": "In Spring Boot 4 with Jackson 3.x, databind types (ObjectMapper, JsonNode, JsonMapper) moved to the tools.jackson.databind package while Jackson annotations remained in com.fasterxml.jackson.annotation; Spring Boot auto-configures a tools.jackson.databind.ObjectMapper bean.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CLAUDE.md#L247-L248",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d02b8bc4144e5079c291dba7193f5a029ff6ccde35a71cf41f34df279b5708ee:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_75024905fe60493391bf49739fcd9945",
      "statement": "In Spring Boot 4, RestClientCustomizer moved from org.springframework.boot.web.client to org.springframework.boot.restclient, and Spring Boot auto-applies any RestClientCustomizer bean to the auto-configured RestClient.Builder injected into services.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CLAUDE.md#L251-L251",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b15a71e51bb4d75e42da98814de063f98e850809933a2a747911a3931bc33ce3:"
        },
        {
